{#
  Self-hosted OBSIDIAN type families. The @font-face rules live in the theme CSS
  (web/css/theme.source.css) and are served from our own origin via Vite — no
  Google Fonts round-trip, no preconnects. font-display:swap keeps text visible
  meanwhile.

  Only the two faces that actually paint are here. Body copy rides the system
  stack: it reads the same and costs nothing, which keeps the display face —
  the one the hero LCP waits on — from queueing behind a second download.

  The display face carries fetchpriority=high because the hero LCP is text set
  in it: without the hint it queues alongside ~70 other downloads and lands over
  a second late, which is exactly what the LCP waits on.

  Mono earns its preload: it dresses the demo bar, the header actions and the
  hero eyebrow, all above the fold, so discovering it from the stylesheet
  repainted half the viewport a second late.
#}
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin fetchpriority="high"
      href="{{ block.getViteFileUrl('bodoni-moda-latin-wght-normal.woff2') }}">
<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin
      href="{{ block.getViteFileUrl('jetbrains-mono-latin-wght-normal.woff2') }}">
